Subject: [PATCH] Embedding changes for ais2api on FIREFOX_158_0_1_RELEASE

Based on AIStudio2API's SpiderMonkey patch (Mag1cFall/firefox e297ff009d,
written for FIREFOX_152_0_4_RELEASE); ais2api maintains it since 158.0.1.

- build/moz.configure/flags.configure: the js project skips the check for
  linking libstdc++ statically.
- intl/components/src/Locale.*: mozjs_set_camou_locale(locale) sets the
  thread's default locale. Unlike the 152 patch, it no longer replaces the
  language and region of every Locale, which made a locale a script names
  itself (new Intl.Locale("fr-FR")) report the embedding's language.
- js/src/build/moz.build: mozglue is linked into the js library.
- js/src/jsapi.cpp, js/src/vm/FrameIter.cpp: scripts compiled with the file
  name "self-hosted" count as self-hosted frames, so host scripts stay out of
  stacks and caller lookups.
- js/src/vm/GlobalObject.*: standard constructors appear in the order scripts
  first use them, and mozjs_delete_global_property removes a global property.

diff -ruN a/build/moz.configure/flags.configure b/build/moz.configure/flags.configure
--- a/build/moz.configure/flags.configure
+++ b/build/moz.configure/flags.configure
@@ -74,7 +74,7 @@
             )
 
 
-@depends(when=link_libstdcxx_statically)
+@depends(when=link_libstdcxx_statically & depends(build_project)(lambda p: p != "js"))
 def check_libstdcxx_linkage():
     die("Firefox does not support linking statically with libstdc++")
 
